Design for Material Degradation Acceptance encourages users to perceive the natural ageing and wear of materials as a positive quality rather than a defect. In a refurbishment context, this strategy reduces premature product replacement driven by cosmetic deterioration, keeping products in use longer and improving the volume and quality of returns entering the refurbishment pipeline. Materials that age gracefully — developing a patina, softening with use, or showing wear patterns that tell a story — can shift user perception from "worn out" to "well-loved".